    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1647" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ăgylla</span></b> , ae,
		f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				town in Etruria</i>, called later Caere, now <i>Cervetri</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 8, 479</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 5,
				8, § 51</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ăgyllīni</span></b> , <i>inhabitants of Agylla</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. A.
				12, 281</span></i>.</div>
